{{media:wxr-5950ax12.jpg?300|Buffalo WXR-5950AX12}}

The Buffalo WXR-5950AX12 / WXR-6000AX12x family of routers feature two 10GbE ports and 802.11ax WiFi on both 2.4GHz @40MHz 4x4 and 5GHz @160MHz 8x8 radios with beam-forming support, for a combined ~6000Mbps wireless throughput.

It is based on the Qualcomm IPQ8074A SoC, AP-HK01-C1 reference design platform. It has three 1GbE LAN ports, one 10GbE LAN port, one 10GbE WAN port and 4 non-detachable external antenna poles, with two physical dipolar antennas in each pole, which are not soldered internally. Buffalo first released the WXR-5950AX12 in late 2019, followed by WXR-6000AX12x refresh models released from 2021 that seem to have the identical hardware ((The WXR-5950AX12 and WXR-6000AX12x variants use different WiFi Board Data File (BDF) and calibration firmware for correctly initializing the 5GHz radio)).

